# R4 golden: `uddeshya` was the keyword for `continue` before v157. It is no
# longer a keyword, so it is a name, and a name that was never declared is a
# compile error. Before R4 this program compiled and printed 0 1 2 3 4 -- the
# `continue` silently did nothing. Expected to FAIL to compile, with a hint
# naming the new keyword.
mukhya() {
    chakra i = 0 tak 4 {
        yadi (i == 2) { uddeshya }
        likha(i)
    }
}
